Package: shapvalues
Type: Package
Title: Fast Model-Agnostic Shapley Additive Explanations
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: person("Imad", "El Badisy", email = "elbadisyimad@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computes Shapley additive explanations (SHAP) for the predictions of
    any supervised model through a single prediction callback, covering
    regression, binary and multiclass classification, and right-censored
    survival analysis with time-dependent attributions. The sampling
    (permutation) estimator of Strumbelj and Kononenko (2014)
    <doi:10.1007/s10115-013-0679-x> is used, with all coalition predictions
    issued in one batched call and the marginal-contribution reduction run in
    parallel 'C++' via 'RcppParallel'. Pairwise interaction values are
    available. A native 'ggplot2' layer provides the usual beeswarm,
    importance, waterfall, dependence and time-curve plots, plus opinionated
    multivariate views (an attribution compass with an explanation
    concentration index, radial fingerprints of explanation phenotypes, and
    attribution pathways), all sharing one colour system with selectable
    'viridisLite' styles.
